<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3299] Cache remove can be lost in ATOMIC cache with OFFHEAP_TIERED memory mode</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3299</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Added test reproducing issue (IgniteCacheConcurrentPutGetRemove).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. There is an issue with &apos;deferredDelete&apos; implementation - entry marked as &apos;deleted&apos; can be evicted from cache, after this information about remove is lost (note: this can be reproduced not only in OFFHEAP_TIERED, but also in ONHEAP_TIERED mode with eviction policy, also this can also cause lost update in transactional cache on changing topology).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. Looks like condition for removing from offheap in GridCacheMapEntry.innerUpdate is not correct:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;            if (op != GridCacheOperation.UPDATE &amp;amp;&amp;amp; cctx.offheapTiered() &amp;amp;&amp;amp; hasValPtr) {
                boolean rmv = cctx.swap().removeOffheap(key);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is possible that value was put in offheap, but &apos;hasValPtr&apos; is false.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
